Several Vim tests assume terminal behavior that is not reliably available when
the test suite is driven through screen(1) on headless build machines:

Test_popup_shadow_hiddenchar(), Test_pumopt_opacity_text_attrs(),
Test_pum_opacity_lowcolor(), and Test_popup_opacity_lowcolor() compare exact
screen dumps for popup shadow/blend rendering.  screen changes the cell
attributes seen by Vim enough that the expected dumps are not stable.

Test_stdin_no_newline() scans the visible shell transcript for the nested Vim
command line.  The command output itself is correct, but under the nested
screen terminal harness the command line is not always retained in the visible
terminal lines.

Test_modifyOtherKeys_shift_tab() and Test_term_keycode_translation() depend on
the exact key encodings reported by the terminal.  screen reports different
encodings for Shift-Tab and Delete than the tests expect.

Test_term_win_resize() relies on terminal resize events that are not propagated
reliably when the test suite runs under screen.

Test_terminal_noblock() unnecessarily delays under the screen harness because
it sends enough echoed data that the shell may not reach "done" before the
test times out.  Use a smaller workload.

Test_aa_terminal_focus_events() sends focus events through the outer terminal
and expects them to reach the inner Vim terminal.  screen does not forward those
events reliably.

